Regional Market Insights
North America: Continues to lead with 42% market share, driven by high ticket prices and extensive touring circuits. The U.S. alone hosts over 30,000 concerts annually across its network of world-class venues.
Europe: Maintains strong festival culture and artist-friendly routing between countries. Germany and the UK account for nearly half of regional revenue.
Asia-Pacific: The fastest-growing region, with K-pop driving stadium sellouts and China's domestic market expanding rapidly despite restrictions on international acts.
Latin America: Brazil and Mexico dominate, though promoters face currency volatility challenges when booking global stars.
